    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0497" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2540/8.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Fox to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-06-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 18,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Fox informs Mr. Root, referring to previous correspondence<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d284-f1"/> eight, twelve, and also fifteen, that the railway crisis
                    is reached, and that revolution is imminent owing to the railway problem. He
                    also states that the American investments are reported as being in danger, the
                    people insisting on confiscation. He further states that the railway company
                    urges arbitration of her contract. He asks for instructions.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
